{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3Mtt4fuZbt4SDSJgGKS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm test` and `npm run size` pass\n\nTicket 08 is done and all six checklist items are checked. Inside a component, writing to a prop that has a signal or computed bound to it now throws. The error names the tag and the prop and says to emit an event instead, and the bound signal keeps its value.\n\n**Why the last attempt failed:** the code was fine. The test runner (tapout) always uses port 8123, and another process held that port, most likely a parallel ticket's test run. This time I waited for the port to free before running the browser suite.\n\n**Code:** the change is in `src/factory.ts`, in the function setup uses for each prop. When a signal is bound, calling it with a value throws. When nothing is bound, the write goes through as before. Assigning to the host's accessor from outside and ignoring attribute changes while bound both work as they did.\n\n**Tests:** I added four to the \"prop accessor\" block in `test/index.ts`:\n1. Writing a prop bound to a signal throws, the message names the tag and prop, and the signal is unchanged.\n2. Writing a prop bound to a computed throws. This failed against the old code, where the write was silently dropped.\n3. A component can still write a prop that has nothing bound to it.\n4. Assigning a new signal from outside replaces the old binding.\n\nTests 3 and 4 also pass on the old code. They protect behaviour the ticket says must not change.\n\n**Docs:** the **Prop** entry in `CONTEXT.md`, ADR-007's Consequences section and the prop accessor section of `AGENTS.md` now say a bound prop is read-only inside the component. I also added two testing pitfalls to `AGENTS.md`: the fixed port, and tapzero's `t.throws` returning a Promise.\n\n**Checks:** after rebuilding `dist/`, `npm test` passes 297/297, and `npm run size` and `npm run lint` pass. Core now measures 4.2 kB against its 4.2 kB limit, so I didn't raise the limit, but there is almost no room left for later tickets.\n\nThere are three commits; `.nightralph/notes.md` is left uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":70312,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"output_tokens":701,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b283c04-55b4-4028-a6ec-f8a0eea1968c","uuid":"486550ad-3dad-4dad-9ebc-8a814e249ae1","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:05:10.901Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Mtsn4937Bnw3zCgGpD"}
